  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard measures",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "# PCA UE \u00b7 Access Endpoint / Session Agent\n\n**Path:** source RedPanda `edr-access-endpoint` \u2192 Go Telemetry Collector with embedded Telegraf \u2192 Roadrunner Gateway \u2192 Fedex \u2192 Kafka `spark_raw_in` \u2192 Ignite \u2192 Spark \u2192 HDFS \u2192 Gather \u2192 Druid. Spark/HDFS/Druid require full analytics.\n\n**Read the units:** Ignite sent counts normalized rows published to Kafka, not individual KPI values or Druid inserts. Agent received counts payload bytes from embedded Telegraf, including its internal metrics. Gather submission counters count requests/tasks, not data rows. Gather panels include all metric object types of the selected tenant; only the Ignite and Druid inventory panels select the PCA UE AP object type.\n\n**Availability and completeness:** UP proves a metrics scrape. Telegraf status proves the embedded process is running. Counters are filtered to currently UP targets; missing lazy counters are not manufactured zero values. Druid inventory comes from Gather's periodic inventory for the previous completed clock hour; current-hour records are excluded. Verify a test run through its actual Druid/Gather query before declaring end-to-end success. Tenant filters apply to data panels; health and agent transport cover configured deployment targets. Configure optional `pcaue-ap-agent` scrape targets to populate the two agent panels.\n\nFor NI flow rows written to ClickHouse, open **PCA UE \u00b7 EDR Ingestion**. Its `pcaueni_*` counters measure the separate NI path."
      }
    },
